From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucas gelfond <lucasgelfond@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] demux: mp4: leave files with IAMF audio to avformat

VLC has no IAMF (Immersive Audio Model and Formats) decoder, and an IAMF
track is not something a decoder could take on its own: its Opus, AAC,
FLAC or PCM substreams are described by the descriptors of the sample
entry. FFmpeg's demuxer exposes those substreams. The MP4 demuxer took
these files anyway and played their video in silence.

When avformat is available, leave files with an IAMF track to it.
---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/demux/mp4/mp4.c b/modules/demux/mp4/mp4.c
--- a/modules/demux/mp4/mp4.c
+++ b/modules/demux/mp4/mp4.c
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@
 #include <vlc_dialog.h>
 #include <vlc_url.h>
 #include <vlc_replay_gain.h>
+#include <vlc_modules.h>
 #include <assert.h>
 #include <limits.h>
 #include <stdckdint.h>
@@ -1400,6 +1401,19 @@ static int Open( vlc_object_t * p_this )
         p_track->i_pts_offset = p_sys->i_max_pts_offset - p_track->i_pts_offset;
     }
 
+    /* There is no IAMF (Immersive Audio) decoder: its audio is only
+     * reachable through FFmpeg's demuxer, which then plays the whole file */
+    for( unsigned i = 0; i < p_sys->i_tracks; i++ )
+    {
+        if( p_sys->track[i].b_ok &&
+            p_sys->track[i].fmt.i_codec == VLC_FOURCC('i','a','m','f') &&
+            module_exists( "avformat" ) )
+        {
+            msg_Dbg( p_demux, "leaving IAMF audio to avformat" );
+            goto error;
+        }
+    }
+
     p_mvex = MP4_BoxGet( p_sys->p_moov, "mvex" );
     if( p_mvex != NULL )
     {
